  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STREAM Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Beni Suef governorate and Cairo city</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities living with the target areas of the project (Beni Suef governorate) and the ERC HQ in Cairo City</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Engagement with local communities, expert organizations and the larger Red Cross Movement is at the core of this project. Local communities will be engaged from the very first moment, both in the landscape assessments and the design and implementation of the pilot interventions. As the natural environment is not a key area of expertise for the Red Cross, we need to engage with expert organizations and other non-Movement partners that know more than we do.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nature, lives, and livelihoods are inextricably linked; where nature is degraded, survival and livelihoods are put at increased risk. Conversely, we experience numerous benefits if nature is protected and restored, such as reduced disaster risk and enhanced food and water security. In Egypt, 95% of the population live within a few kilometers of the Nile river, and their livelihoods are dependent on a healthy river ecosystem. Historically agriculture along the river has lived in partnership with the river&#x2019;s regular flooding for improving soil conditions, and water availability for irrigation. However, some agricultural lands are increasingly under stress due to poor soil conditions, salination, and reduced river flow in the Nile river. This may lead to reduced agricultural outputs, reducing reliable income and increasing (staple) food prices, for the most vulnerable groups.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this project is to test and scale Nature-based Solutions as a tool for humanitarian organizations to reduce disaster risks and support livelihoods that are suitable to a healthy ecosystem. The end goal is that people become safer in the face of natural hazards and other shocks. Nature-based Solutions can contribute to this, together with other interventions such as improved water management, and Disaster Risk Reduction, that will be included in the project. We believe that Nature-based Solutions contribute to three strongly interrelated goals that together reduce disaster risks: healthy ecosystems, safe communities, and economic opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
